# Retrieving Interfaces from a GraphQL Endpoint

You can retrieve interfaces from a GraphQL endpoint using **introspection queries**. Here are the main approaches:

## 1. Query All Interfaces

```graphql
{
  __schema {
    types {
      kind
      name
      description
    }
  }
}
```

Filter results where `kind == "INTERFACE"`.

## 2. Query Interfaces with Their Fields

```graphql
{
  __schema {
    types {
      kind
      name
      fields {
        name
        type {
          name
          kind
        }
      }
      possibleTypes {
        name
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## 3. Query a Specific Interface

```graphql
{
  __type(name: "Node") {
    kind
    name
    fields {
      name
      type {
        name
        kind
      }
    }
    possibleTypes {
      name
      kind
    }
  }
}
```

## 4. Using cURL

```bash
curl -X POST https://your-endpoint.com/graphql \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"query": "{ __schema { types { kind name } } }"}'
```

## 5. Using Tools

- **GraphiQL / GraphQL Playground / Apollo Sandbox** – built-in schema explorer
- **`graphql-cli`** – `graphql get-schema` to download the full schema
- **`apollo-cli`** – `apollo schema:download`
- **`get-graphql-schema`** – `npx get-graphql-schema https://endpoint.com/graphql > schema.graphql`

## 6. Full Introspection Query

For a complete schema dump including all interfaces:

```graphql
query IntrospectionQuery {
  __schema {
    types {
      kind
      name
      interfaces { name }
      possibleTypes { name }
      fields {
        name
        type { name kind }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Note on Disabled Introspection

Many production servers **disable introspection** for security. If so, you'll need:
- Access to the schema file (SDL) from developers
- Tools like **Clairvoyance** or **GraphQL Cop** to infer the schema
- Documentation provided by the API owner

